Given differential equation is

$\begin{aligned}$& $\left( x^2-1\right) \frac{d y}{d x}$+$2 x y=x \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{d y}{d x}+\frac{2 x}{x^2-1} \cdot y=\frac{x}{x^2-1}
\end{aligned}$ This is in linear form.

$\begin{aligned}$& $\text{ Integrating factor }=\int\frac{2 x}{x^2-1} d$ x=\int_e $\frac{d t}{t}$\\
& $\text{$ where } \begin{aligned}$& =x²-1 \\
& =e^{\log t}=x²-1
\end{aligned}
\end{aligned}

Hence, required integrating factor $=x^2-1$.$

